  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I think an advance submenu for users to adjust avatars might be interesting and good for optimization. This advanced submenu is where users can toggle buttons to adjust avatar parameters. This can be how much a player is bright or dark; perhaps how their materials are displayed. Perhaps there can be a list of all the materials of an avatar one can turn on and off. Maybe there can be a feature where it just shows the avatar's albedo map with no normals, spec, transparency, or emmisive added. We can incorporate an LOD system for avatars where the farther away they are the more they optimize in geometry. Perhaps even have a one poly (double sided) compressed 2D version of a 3D model (it's a weird idea but might prove effective for optimization while still seeing what players fully look like; it's just an idea). We can also set parameters to adjust dynamic bones and colliders. Perhaps have a feature to only turn on avatars that enter within a certain range (they are fully loaded but appear as robots outside your range); the range can also be adjusted. There can also be a reset button to where a player can reset all the parameters. Overall this submenu gives a lot more control over other people's avatars and performance strategies.",
